{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וישמע יתרו", :translit "vayishma yitro", :gloss "And Jethro heard"} {:he "וינהום עליו", :translit "veyenahemu alav", :gloss "and they shall roar over him"} {:he "כנהמת ים", :translit "kenahamat yam", :gloss "like the roaring of the sea"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic interpretation: the sound of the sea splitting traveled to all the kings"}], :frame {:text "Rabbi Eliezer HaGadol says Jethro heard of the splitting of the Sea of Reeds; Rabbi Joshua says he heard of the war with Amalek (Zevahim 116a, Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Amalek 1). The verse 'shall the sea roar' (Psalms 96:11) and the roar 'like the roaring of the sea' (Isaiah 17:12) are cited as proof that the splitting produced a sound heard far and wide.", :sources ["Zevahim 116a" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael Amalek 1" "Psalms 96:11" "Isaiah 17:12"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וישמע יתרו כהן מדין חתן", :translit "vayishma yitro kohen midyan hoten", :gloss "And Jethro heard, priest of Midian, father-in-law"} {:he "אלה הם קריעת הים ומלחמת עמלק", :translit "eleh hem kri'at hayam umilchemet amalek", :gloss "these are the splitting of the sea and the war of Amalek"} {:he "כומר", :translit "kumar", :gloss "priest (of idolatry)"} {:he "התורה", :translit "hatorah", :gloss "the Torah"} {:he "יתרו", :translit "yitro", :gloss "Jethro"} {:he "יתר ו'", :translit "yeter vav", :gloss "extra vav"} {:he "תר\"ו", :translit "tarvav", :gloss "606"} {:he "את כל אשר עשה אלהים למשה", :translit "et kol asher asah elohim lemoshe", :gloss "all that Elohim had done for Moses"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "וישמע יתרו כהן מדין חתן", :b "אלה הם קריעת הים ומלחמת עמלק"} {:kind :gematria, :a "יתרו", :b "כומר"} {:kind :gematria, :a "יתרו", :b "התורה"} {:kind :notarikon, :word "יתרו", :expansion ["יתר" "ו'"]} {:kind :notarikon, :word "יתרו", :expansion ["י' דברות" "תר\"ו מצות"]}], :frame {:text "The Talmud records that Jethro had seven names (Sotah 34a, Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael, Yitro 1). Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael states he was originally a priest of idolatry. The RI'A (Rabbi Yeshaya of Trani) and the Rosh are medieval authorities whose explanations Ba'al HaTurim cites. The Noahide commandments numbering seven are discussed in Sanhedrin 56a. Jethro's conversion to accept the Torah follows the sequence described in the chapter.", :sources ["Sotah 34a" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael Yitro 1" "Sanhedrin 56a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אלהים", :translit "elohim", :gloss "God / god / judge"} {:he "שר", :translit "sar", :gloss "prince"} {:he "ויפגשהו ה' ויבקש המיתו", :translit "vayifgeshehu Hashem vayevakesh hamito", :gloss "and HaShem met him and sought to put him to death"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading: 'elohim' over Pharaoh means Moses was made a prince/master over Pharaoh"} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading: the attribute of judgment ('elohim') nearly killed Moses for delaying circumcision"}], :frame {:text "God tells Moses, 'See I have made you elohim to Pharaoh' (Exodus 7:1), interpreted by Rashi citing Shemot Rabbah 8:1 to mean a master and judge. The incident at the inn where God sought to kill Moses for not circumcising his son is narrated in Exodus 4:24; Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael connects this to the same attribute of judgment.", :sources ["Exodus 7:1" "Exodus 4:24" "Shemot Rabbah 8:1" "Mekhilta de-Rabbi Yishmael Yitro 1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "עשה אלהים", :translit "asah elohim", :gloss "done [by] God / God has done"} {:he "מה זאת עשה אלהים לנו", :translit "mah zot asah elohim lanu", :gloss "What is this that God has done to us"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["עשה אלהים"]}], :frame {:text "The two occurrences of 'עשה אלהים' are linked by the standard Masoretic principle that rare identical phrases establish a thematic correspondence. In Genesis 42:28, the brothers cry out 'What is this that God has done to us?' in distress when they discover the returned money; Ba'al HaTurim reads their eventual benefit from that distress as corresponding to the redemption language of Exodus 18:1.", :sources ["Genesis 42:28" "Exodus 18:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Midrashic interpretation: the sound of the sea splitting traveled to all the kings", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:a-value 1679, :b-value 1680, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "אלה הם קריעת הים ומלחמת עמלק", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "וישמע יתרו כהן מדין חתן"} {:kind :gematria, :a "יתרו", :a-value 616, :b "כומר", :b-value 266, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "יתרו", :a-value 616, :b "התורה", :b-value 616, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :notarikon, :word "יתרו", :expansion ["יתר" "ו'"], :initials ["י" "ו"], :by :selah, :initials-match? false} {:kind :notarikon, :word "יתרו", :expansion ["י' דברות" "תר\"ו מצות"], :initials ["י" "ת"], :by :selah, :initials-match? false} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading: 'elohim' over Pharaoh means Moses was made a prince/master over Pharaoh", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Midrashic reading: the attribute of judgment ('elohim') nearly killed Moses for delaying circumcision", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["עשה אלהים"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "עשה אלהים", :refs ["Genesis 42:28" "Exodus 18:1"], :n 2, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:17:14.080048483Z", :model "glm-5.2"}